{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QMneKM6ubWpdPxCoNaZzfX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\\documentclass[11pt]{amsart}\n     2→\\usepackage{amsmath,amsthm,amssymb,bm}\n     3→\\usepackage{xcolor}\n     4→\\usepackage{indentfirst}\n     5→\\usepackage{graphicx}\n     6→\\usepackage{tikz}\n     7→\\usetikzlibrary{decorations.pathreplacing, decorations.pathmorphing, decorations.shapes}\n     8→\\usetikzlibrary{arrows,calc}\n     9→\\usepackage{mathrsfs,esint}\n    10→\\usepackage{comment}\n    11→\\usepackage{enumerate}\n    12→\\usepackage{hyperref}\n    13→\\hypersetup{\n    14→    colorlinks = true,\n    15→    linkcolor = red,\n    16→    anchorcolor = green!50!black,\n    17→    citecolor = green!50!black,\n    18→    filecolor = green!50!black,\n    19→    urlcolor = green!50!black\n    20→}\n    21→\\usepackage{cleveref}\n    22→\n    23→\\usepackage[top=1in, bottom=1in, left=1.25in, right=1.25in]{geometry}\n    24→\\usepackage{setspace}\n    25→\n    26→\\usepackage{float}\n    27→\n    28→\\usepackage{subcaption}\n    29→\\usepackage{pgfplots}\n    30→\\pgfplotsset{compat=newest, compat/show suggested version=false}\n    31→\\usepackage{tikz}\n    32→\\usetikzlibrary{intersections}\n    33→\n    34→\\usepackage{diagbox}\n    35→\\usepackage{algorithm, algorithmicx, algpseudocode}\n    36→\\numberwithin{algorithm}{section}\n    37→\\usepackage{tabularx}\n    38→\\usepackage{tcolorbox}\n    39→\n    40→\\usepackage[titletoc,toc,title]{appendix}\n    41→\\renewcommand\\appendixname{Appendix}\n    42→\n    43→\\newtheorem{thm}{Theorem}[section]\n    44→\\newtheorem{theorem}[thm]{Theorem}\n    45→\\newtheorem{proposition}[thm]{Proposition}\n    46→\\newtheorem{corollary}[thm]{Corollary}\n    47→\\newtheorem{lemma}[thm]{Lemma}\n    48→\\newtheorem{remark}[thm]{\\textit{Remark}}\n    49→\\newtheorem{definition}[thm]{Definition}\n    50→\\newtheorem{assumption}[thm]{Assumption}\n    51→\\newtheorem{example}[thm]{Example}\n    52→\n    53→\\newcommand{\\titleShort}{Wave PINNs}\n    54→\\newcommand{\\titleLong}{Precise Goal and Verification Conditions for the Weight Construction}\n    55→\n    56→\\title[\\titleShort]{\\titleLong}\n    57→\n    58→\\thanks{}\n    59→\n    60→\\author{Author}\n    61→% \\address{Address}\n    62→% \\email{Email}\n    63→\n    64→\\date{}\n    65→\n    66→% \\renewcommand \\theequation {\\arabic{section}.\\arabic{equation}}\n    67→\\numberwithin{equation}{section}\n    68→\n    69→\\begin{document}\n    70→% \\maketitle\n    71→\n    72→%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n    73→\\section{Precise Goal}\n    74→\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=green!5, colframe=green!75!blue, title=Goal with necessary conditions]\n    75→For given arbitrary wave speed $c > 0$ and terminal time $T > 0$, find\n    76→\\begin{equation*}\n    77→    \\left\\{\n    78→    \\begin{aligned}\n    79→        &\\psi(x, t) && \\text{function of $x$ and $t$},\\\\\n    80→        &s          && \\text{negative constant},\\\\\n    81→        &\\alpha     && \\text{constant},\\\\\n    82→        &\\lambda    && \\text{constant},\n    83→    \\end{aligned}\n    84→    \\right.\n    85→\\end{equation*}\n    86→such that the following necessary conditions are satisfied for all $(x, t) \\in [0, \\infty) \\times [0, T]$\n    87→\\begin{equation*}\n    88→    \\left\\{\n    89→    \\begin{aligned}\n    90→        &L_{1} \\psi < L \\psi < - L_{1} \\psi,\\\\\n    91→        &\\lim_{x \\to + \\infty} \\lambda \\psi = + \\infty,\\\\\n    92→        &L_{2} \\psi > 0.\n    93→    \\end{aligned}\n    94→    \\right.\n    95→\\end{equation*}\n    96→\\end{tcolorbox}\n    97→\n    98→\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=orange!5, colframe=orange!80!blue, title=Sufficient condition]\n    99→The final verification concerns the sufficient condition for all $(x, t) \\in [0, \\infty) \\times [0, T]$\n   100→\\begin{equation*}\n   101→    (L_{1} \\psi)^{2} - (L \\psi)^{2}\n   102→    \\geq\n   103→    c^{2} (\\partial_{x, t}^{2} \\varphi)^{2}.\n   104→\\end{equation*}\n   105→\\end{tcolorbox}\n   106→\n   107→\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=blue!5, colframe=blue!70, title=Definitions and notations]\n   108→\\begin{enumerate}\n   109→    \\item $\\varphi$: function of $x$ and $t$,\n   110→    \\begin{equation*}\n   111→        \\varphi\n   112→        =\n   113→        \\exp(\\lambda \\psi).\n   114→    \\end{equation*}\n   115→\n   116→    \\item $\\square$: operator acting on functions of $x$ and $t$,\n   117→    \\begin{equation*}\n   118→        \\square u\n   119→        =\n   120→        \\partial_{t}^{2} u - c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} u.\n   121→    \\end{equation*}\n   122→\n   123→    \\item $\\widetilde{\\square}$: operator acting on functions of $x$ and $t$,\n   124→    \\begin{equation*}\n   125→        \\widetilde{\\square} u\n   126→        =\n   127→        |\\partial_{t} u|^{2} - c^{2}|\\partial_{x} u|^{2}.\n   128→    \\end{equation*}\n   129→\n   130→    \\item $L$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n   131→    \\begin{equation*}\n   132→        L \\psi\n   133→        =\n   134→        \\lambda^{2} \\varphi (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)\n   135→        -\n   136→        (\\alpha - 1) \\lambda \\varphi (\\square \\psi).\n   137→    \\end{equation*}\n   138→\n   139→    \\item $L_{1}$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n   140→    \\begin{equation*}\n   141→        \\begin{aligned}\n   142→            L_{1} \\psi\n   143→            &=\n   144→            c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} \\varphi\n   145→            +\n   146→            \\partial_{t}^{2} \\varphi\\\\\n   147→            &=\n   148→            \\lambda^{2} \\varphi\n   149→            \\left (\n   150→                (\\partial_{t} \\psi)^{2}\n   151→                +\n   152→                c^{2} (\\partial_{x} \\psi)^{2}\n   153→            \\right )\n   154→            +\n   155→            \\lambda \\varphi\n   156→            \\left (\n   157→                \\partial_{t}^{2} \\psi\n   158→                +\n   159→                c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} \\psi\n   160→            \\right ).\n   161→        \\end{aligned}\n   162→    \\end{equation*}\n   163→\n   164→    \\item $L_{2}$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n   165→    \\begin{equation*}\n   166→    \\begin{aligned}\n   167→        L_{2}\n   168→        &=\n   169→        \\frac{1}{2}\n   170→        \\Big (\n   171→            (\\alpha - 1) s \\lambda (\\square (\\varphi (\\square \\psi)))\n   172→            -\n   173→            s \\lambda^{2} (\\square (\\varphi (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)))\n   174→        \\Big )\\\\\n   175→        &+\n   176→        \\Big (\n   177→            s^{3} \\lambda^{3} (\\alpha - 1) \\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\square \\psi)\n   178→            -\n   179→            s^{3} \\lambda^{4} \\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)^{2}\\\\\n   180→            &\\qquad+\n   181→            s^{3} \\lambda^{3}\n   182→            \\left (\n   183→                \\partial_{t} (\\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\partial_{t} \\psi))\n   184→                +\n   185→                c^{2} \\partial_{x}(\\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\partial_{x} \\psi))\n   186→            \\right )\n   187→        \\Big ).\n   188→    \\end{aligned}\n   189→    \\end{equation*}\n   190→\\end{enumerate}\n   191→\\end{tcolorbox}\n   192→Note that $\\partial_{x}^{2} u = \\partial_{x} (\\partial_{x} u) = u_{x x}$.\n   193→This problem comes from the Carleman estimate for the wave operator $\\square$.\n   194→$\\psi, s, \\alpha, \\lambda$ could be dependent on $c$ and $T$.\n   195→If multiple $\\psi$ are possible, find the smoothest one.\n   196→\n   197→\\end{document}\n   198→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6971574-08be-4f62-adc7-c296c2d3da58","uuid":"f13d05f5-7e61-4007-946b-cae0ac7a75d0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/local/home/cyanz/wave_PINN/problem.tex","content":"\\documentclass[11pt]{amsart}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amsthm,amssymb,bm}\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage{indentfirst}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{tikz}\n\\usetikzlibrary{decorations.pathreplacing, decorations.pathmorphing, decorations.shapes}\n\\usetikzlibrary{arrows,calc}\n\\usepackage{mathrsfs,esint}\n\\usepackage{comment}\n\\usepackage{enumerate}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\hypersetup{\n    colorlinks = true,\n    linkcolor = red,\n    anchorcolor = green!50!black,\n    citecolor = green!50!black,\n    filecolor = green!50!black,\n    urlcolor = green!50!black\n}\n\\usepackage{cleveref}\n\n\\usepackage[top=1in, bottom=1in, left=1.25in, right=1.25in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{setspace}\n\n\\usepackage{float}\n\n\\usepackage{subcaption}\n\\usepackage{pgfplots}\n\\pgfplotsset{compat=newest, compat/show suggested version=false}\n\\usepackage{tikz}\n\\usetikzlibrary{intersections}\n\n\\usepackage{diagbox}\n\\usepackage{algorithm, algorithmicx, algpseudocode}\n\\numberwithin{algorithm}{section}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\usepackage{tcolorbox}\n\n\\usepackage[titletoc,toc,title]{appendix}\n\\renewcommand\\appendixname{Appendix}\n\n\\newtheorem{thm}{Theorem}[section]\n\\newtheorem{theorem}[thm]{Theorem}\n\\newtheorem{proposition}[thm]{Proposition}\n\\newtheorem{corollary}[thm]{Corollary}\n\\newtheorem{lemma}[thm]{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{remark}[thm]{\\textit{Remark}}\n\\newtheorem{definition}[thm]{Definition}\n\\newtheorem{assumption}[thm]{Assumption}\n\\newtheorem{example}[thm]{Example}\n\n\\newcommand{\\titleShort}{Wave PINNs}\n\\newcommand{\\titleLong}{Precise Goal and Verification Conditions for the Weight Construction}\n\n\\title[\\titleShort]{\\titleLong}\n\n\\thanks{}\n\n\\author{Author}\n% \\address{Address}\n% \\email{Email}\n\n\\date{}\n\n% \\renewcommand \\theequation {\\arabic{section}.\\arabic{equation}}\n\\numberwithin{equation}{section}\n\n\\begin{document}\n% \\maketitle\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\\section{Precise Goal}\n\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=green!5, colframe=green!75!blue, title=Goal with necessary conditions]\nFor given arbitrary wave speed $c > 0$ and terminal time $T > 0$, find\n\\begin{equation*}\n    \\left\\{\n    \\begin{aligned}\n        &\\psi(x, t) && \\text{function of $x$ and $t$},\\\\\n        &s          && \\text{negative constant},\\\\\n        &\\alpha     && \\text{constant},\\\\\n        &\\lambda    && \\text{constant},\n    \\end{aligned}\n    \\right.\n\\end{equation*}\nsuch that the following necessary conditions are satisfied for all $(x, t) \\in [0, \\infty) \\times [0, T]$\n\\begin{equation*}\n    \\left\\{\n    \\begin{aligned}\n        &L_{1} \\psi < L \\psi < - L_{1} \\psi,\\\\\n        &\\lim_{x \\to + \\infty} \\lambda \\psi = + \\infty,\\\\\n        &L_{2} \\psi > 0.\n    \\end{aligned}\n    \\right.\n\\end{equation*}\n\\end{tcolorbox}\n\n\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=orange!5, colframe=orange!80!blue, title=Sufficient condition]\nThe final verification concerns the sufficient condition for all $(x, t) \\in [0, \\infty) \\times [0, T]$\n\\begin{equation*}\n    (L_{1} \\psi)^{2} - (L \\psi)^{2}\n    \\geq\n    c^{2} (\\partial_{x, t}^{2} \\varphi)^{2}.\n\\end{equation*}\n\\end{tcolorbox}\n\n\\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=blue!5, colframe=blue!70, title=Definitions and notations]\n\\begin{enumerate}\n    \\item $\\varphi$: function of $x$ and $t$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n        \\varphi\n        =\n        \\exp(\\lambda \\psi).\n    \\end{equation*}\n\n    \\item $\\square$: operator acting on functions of $x$ and $t$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n        \\square u\n        =\n        \\partial_{t}^{2} u - c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} u.\n    \\end{equation*}\n\n    \\item $\\widetilde{\\square}$: operator acting on functions of $x$ and $t$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n        \\widetilde{\\square} u\n        =\n        |\\partial_{t} u|^{2} - c^{2}|\\partial_{x} u|^{2}.\n    \\end{equation*}\n\n    \\item $L$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n        L \\psi\n        =\n        \\lambda^{2} \\varphi (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)\n        -\n        (\\alpha - 1) \\lambda \\varphi (\\square \\psi).\n    \\end{equation*}\n\n    \\item $L_{1}$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n        \\begin{aligned}\n            L_{1} \\psi\n            &=\n            c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} \\varphi\n            +\n            \\partial_{t}^{2} \\varphi\\\\\n            &=\n            \\lambda^{2} \\varphi\n            \\left (\n                (\\partial_{t} \\psi)^{2}\n                +\n                c^{2} (\\partial_{x} \\psi)^{2}\n            \\right )\n            +\n            \\lambda \\varphi\n            \\left (\n                \\partial_{t}^{2} \\psi\n                +\n                c^{2} \\partial_{x}^{2} \\psi\n            \\right ).\n        \\end{aligned}\n    \\end{equation*}\n\n    \\item $L_{2}$: operator acting on $\\psi$,\n    \\begin{equation*}\n    \\begin{aligned}\n        L_{2}\n        &=\n        \\frac{1}{2}\n        \\Big (\n            (\\alpha - 1) s \\lambda (\\square (\\varphi (\\square \\psi)))\n            -\n            s \\lambda^{2} (\\square (\\varphi (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)))\n        \\Big )\\\\\n        &+\n        \\Big (\n            s^{3} \\lambda^{3} (\\alpha - 1) \\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\square \\psi)\n            -\n            s^{3} \\lambda^{4} \\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi)^{2}\\\\\n            &\\qquad+\n            s^{3} \\lambda^{3}\n            \\left (\n                \\partial_{t} (\\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\partial_{t} \\psi))\n                +\n                c^{2} \\partial_{x}(\\varphi^{3} (\\widetilde{\\square} \\psi) (\\partial_{x} \\psi))\n            \\right )\n        \\Big ).\n    \\end{aligned}\n    \\end{equation*}\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{tcolorbox}\nNote that $\\partial_{x}^{2} u = \\partial_{x} (\\partial_{x} u) = u_{x x}$.\nThis problem comes from the Carleman estimate for the wave operator $\\square$.\n$\\psi, s, \\alpha, \\lambda$ could be dependent on $c$ and $T$.\nIf multiple $\\psi$ are possible, find the smoothest one.\n\n\\end{document}\n","numLines":198,"startLine":1,"totalLines":198}}}
