{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01H5UGRkkdf8z4ramcUKP2QS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me reason through the mathematical conditions carefully.\n\n**Analysis of the conditions:**\n\n**Condition 2** (easiest to satisfy): `lim_{x→∞} λψ = +∞`. If ψ contains a `-x²` term and λ < 0, then λψ ~ +x² → +∞. ✓\n\n**Condition 1**: `L₁ψ ≤ 0` (as a consequence). We need:\n`λ²((ψ_t)² + c²(ψ_x)²) + λ(ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx) ≤ 0`\n\nFor ψ = a·t - b·(x + x₀)², with λ < 0:\n- ψ_t = a, ψ_x = -2b(x+x₀), ψ_tt = 0, ψ_xx = -2b\n- (ψ_t)² + c²(ψ_x)² = a² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²\n- ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx = -2bc²\n- L₁ψ/φ = λ²(a² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²) + λ(-2bc²)\n  = λ²a² + 4λ²b²c²(x+x₀)² - 2λbc²\n\nWith λ < 0: the first two terms are positive, and -2λbc² > 0 (since λ < 0, b > 0). So L₁ψ/φ > 0, which violates condition 1.\n\nThe problem is the gradient-squared term is always positive. We need λ(ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx) to be negative enough. With λ < 0 and ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx = -2bc², we get λ(-2bc²) = -2λbc² > 0. This adds to the positive gradient term instead of opposing it.\n\nWe need λ(ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx) < 0, i.e., ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx > 0 (since λ < 0). So we need ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx > 0 and large enough.\n\nFor ψ = a·t² - b·(x + x₀)²:\n- ψ_tt = 2a, ψ_xx = -2b\n- ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx = 2a - 2bc²\n- Need this > 0, so a > bc²\n- ψ_t = 2at, ψ_x = -2b(x+x₀)\n- (ψ_t)² + c²(ψ_x)² = 4a²t² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²\n\nL₁ψ/φ = λ²(4a²t² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²) + λ(2a - 2bc²)\n\nFor this to be ≤ 0: λ(2a - 2bc²) must dominate -λ² times the gradient term.\nWith λ < 0 and (2a - 2bc²) > 0: λ(2a - 2bc²) < 0. ✓ This goes the right direction!\n\nWe need: |λ|(2a - 2bc²) ≥ λ²(4a²t² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²)\ni.e., (2a - 2bc²)/|λ| ≥ 4a²t² + 4b²c²(x+x₀)²\n\nThis needs the RHS to be bounded, which it isn't as x→∞. So this simple quadratic won't work either for condition 1 alone.\n\nLet me think differently. The key insight is that the gradient-squared term grows with x² while the Laplacian term is constant for a quadratic ψ. We need the Laplacian to grow with x too, or we need to cancel the gradient growth.\n\n**New idea**: ψ = a·t² + b·t - d·x (linear in x!).\n- ψ_t = 2at + b, ψ_x = -d, ψ_tt = 2a, ψ_xx = 0\n- (ψ_t)² + c²(ψ_x)² = (2at+b)² + c²d²\n- ψ_tt + c²ψ_xx = 2a\n- L₁ψ/φ = λ²((2at+b)² + c²d²) + 2aλ\n- For condition 2: λψ = λ(at² + bt - dx) → +∞ as x→∞ requires λd > 0 (i.e., d < 0 if λ < 0, or d > 0 if λ > 0).\n\nWait, if ψ is linear in x, (ψ_x)² = d² is constant. Then L₁ψ/φ = λ²((2at+b)² + c²d²) + 2aλ. For t ∈ [0,T], the maximum of (2at+b)² is at t=T: (2aT+b)². So we need:\n\n2a|λ| ≥ λ²((2aT+b)² + c²d²)\n\nThis is satisfiable if |λ| is small enough! Specifically |λ| ≤ 2a / ((2aT+b)² + c²d²).\n\nBut we also need condition 2: if ψ = at² + bt - dx with d > 0, then λψ → -λd·x as x→∞. For λ < 0: -λd·x = |λ|d·x → +∞. ✓\n\nNow let me work through the full conditions. Let me use ψ = s₀·t² - d·x where d > 0, s₀ > 0, λ < 0.\n\nActually, let me try a very clean approach: **ψ = t - (x + x₀)** (linear). No, the gradient squared = 1 + c², Laplacian = 0. No Laplacian to help.\n\nLet me try **ψ = a(T-t)² - (x+x₀)** with a > 0, x₀ > 0, λ < 0.\n\nActually, let me try to do this computationally using SymPy to verify my reasoning before committing."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":255,"cache_read_input_tokens":104189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":255,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6971574-08be-4f62-adc7-c296c2d3da58","uuid":"6d7ca2ad-e6eb-4f68-bc39-886f684599f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01H5UGRkkdf8z4ramcUKP2QS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TCpsRJrUEKzVa7E8kvFy5m","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"conda run -n wave python3 -c \"\nimport sympy as sp\n\nx, t = sp.symbols('x t', real=True)\nc = sp.symbols('c', positive=True)\nT_sym = sp.symbols('T', positive=True)\na_sym, b_sym, d_sym = sp.symbols('a b d', positive=True)\nlam_sym = sp.symbols('lam', negative=True)\n\n# Try psi = a*t^2 + b*t - d*x\npsi = a_sym*t**2 + b_sym*t - d_sym*x\n\npsi_t = sp.diff(psi, t)\npsi_x = sp.diff(psi, x)\npsi_tt = sp.diff(psi, t, 2)\npsi_xx = sp.diff(psi, x, 2)\n\nprint('psi_t =', psi_t)\nprint('psi_x =', psi_x)\nprint('psi_tt =', psi_tt)\nprint('psi_xx =', psi_xx)\n\n# Gradient squared (with c)\ngrad_sq = psi_t**2 + c**2 * psi_x**2\nprint('grad_sq =', sp.expand(grad_sq))\n\n# Laplacian-like term\nlap = psi_tt + c**2 * psi_xx\nprint('lap =', lap)\n\n# tilde_square psi = psi_t^2 - c^2 * psi_x^2\ntsq = psi_t**2 - c**2 * psi_x**2\nprint('tilde_square psi =', sp.expand(tsq))\n\n# square psi = psi_tt - c^2 * psi_xx\nsq = psi_tt - c**2 * psi_xx\nprint('square psi =', sq)\n\n# L1 psi / phi = lam^2 * grad_sq + lam * lap\nL1_over_phi = lam_sym**2 * grad_sq + lam_sym * lap\nprint('L1/phi =', sp.expand(L1_over_phi))\nprint('  = lam^2*((2at+b)^2 + c^2*d^2) + 2a*lam')\n\n# For L1/phi <= 0:\n# lam^2*((2at+b)^2 + c^2*d^2) + 2a*lam <= 0\n# Since lam < 0, |lam| = -lam, lam^2 = |lam|^2\n# |lam|^2*(grad) - 2a*|lam| <= 0\n# |lam|*(|lam|*grad - 2a) <= 0\n# Since |lam| > 0: |lam|*grad <= 2a, i.e. |lam| <= 2a/grad\n# Max of grad on [0,inf)x[0,T] = (2aT+b)^2 + c^2*d^2 at t=T, any x\n# So need |lam| <= 2a / ((2aT+b)^2 + c^2*d^2)\n\n# L psi / phi = lam^2 * tsq - (alpha-1)*lam*sq\nalpha_sym = sp.Symbol('alpha')\nL_over_phi = lam_sym**2 * tsq - (alpha_sym - 1)*lam_sym*sq\nprint('L/phi =', sp.expand(L_over_phi))\nprint('  = lam^2*((2at+b)^2 - c^2*d^2) - (alpha-1)*lam*2a')\n\n# For condition 1: L1 <= L <= -L1\n# L - L1 >= 0:\n# L/phi - L1/phi = lam^2*(tsq - grad_sq) - (alpha-1)*lam*sq - lam*lap + ... \n# Wait, let me compute directly\nLmL1 = sp.expand(L_over_phi - L1_over_phi)\nprint('(L - L1)/phi =', LmL1)\n\nmL1mL = sp.expand(-L1_over_phi - L_over_phi)\nprint('(-L1 - L)/phi =', mL1mL)\n\"\n","description":"Symbolic exploration of candidate psi","timeout":30000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":255,"cache_read_input_tokens":104189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":255,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6971574-08be-4f62-adc7-c296c2d3da58","uuid":"88b28410-68f5-49d6-9f82-a08e30b7065e"}
