) - c^2). Negative if c > 1 and t != 0!\n# So cond 1a fails at x=0 for c > 1 with alpha=1. BAD.\n#\n# With alpha > 1:\n# (L-L1)/phi = -2c^2*lam^2*psi_x^2 + |lam|*((alpha-1)*sq + lap)\n# = |lam|*(-2c^2|lam|*x^2/(1+x^2) + (alpha-1)*(1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)) + 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2))\n# = |lam|*(alpha/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + (alpha-2)*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2) - 2c^2|lam|*x^2/(1+x^2))\n# Wait let me redo: sq = psi_tt - c^2*psi_xx = 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# lap = 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# (alpha-1)*sq + lap = (alpha-1)*(sq) + lap = (alpha-1+1)/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + ((alpha-1)-1)*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# = alpha/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + (alpha-2)*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n\n# For alpha=2: = 2/(1+t^2)^(3/2) > 0 always! The x term vanishes!\n# Then (L-L1)/phi = |lam|*(2/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - 2c^2|lam|*x^2/(1+x^2))\n# = 2|lam|*(1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - c^2|lam|*x^2/(1+x^2))\n# At t=0: 1 - c^2|lam|*x^2/(1+x^2). Since x^2/(1+x^2) < 1, this is > 1-c^2|lam|.\n# Positive if |lam| < 1/c^2. ✓\n# At x->inf: 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - c^2|lam|. Positive if 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) > c^2|lam|.\n# i.e., (1+t^2)^(3/2) < 1/(c^2|lam|).\n# For |lam| = 1/(2c^2): (1+t^2)^(3/2) < 2. i.e., t^2 < 2^(2/3)-1 ≈ 0.587. Fails for t > 0.77.\n# For |lam| = 1/(100c^2): (1+t^2)^(3/2) < 100. t^2 < 100^(2/3)-1 ≈ 20.5. t < 4.5.\n# Still fails symbolically (for all t).\n\n# Hmm. The x^2/(1+x^2) term approaches 1, so (L-L1)/phi at x=inf, large t -> negative.\n\n# But what about condition 1b with alpha=2?\n# (L1+L)/phi = 2*lam^2*pt^2 + lam*((2-alpha)*ptt + alpha*c^2*pxx)\n# With alpha=2: = 2*lam^2*t^2/(1+t^2) + lam*(0 + 2c^2*(-1/(1+x^2)^(3/2)))\n# = 2*lam^2*t^2/(1+t^2) - 2c^2|lam|/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# Need <= 0: 2c^2|lam|/(1+x^2)^(3/2) >= 2lam^2*t^2/(1+t^2)\n# i.e., c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2) >= |lam|*t^2/(1+t^2)\n# At x=0: c^2 >= |lam|*t^2/(1+t^2). Since t^2/(1+t^2) < 1: c^2 >= |lam|. OK if |lam| <= c^2.\n# At x=0, t->inf: c^2 >= |lam|. Same.\n# At x->inf: c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2) -> 0 < |lam|*something. FAILS!\n\n# So condition 1b also fails for large x. \n\n# What if alpha is between 1 and 2?\n# (2-alpha)*ptt is positive (since 0 < 2-alpha < 1 and ptt > 0).\n# alpha*c^2*pxx is negative (pxx < 0).\n# (L1+L)/phi = 2lam^2*pt^2 + lam*((2-alpha)/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - alpha*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2))\n# = 2|lam|^2*t^2/(1+t^2) - |lam|*((2-alpha)/(1+t^2)^(3/2) - alpha*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2))\n# = 2|lam|^2*t^2/(1+t^2) - |lam|*(2-alpha)/(1+t^2)^(3/2) + |lam|*alpha*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# Need all <= 0. But the last term is always positive! So L1+L can't be <= 0.\n# Unless the second term (negative) dominates. But the third term |lam|*alpha*c^2/(1+x^2)^(3/2)\n# is positive and doesn't go to 0 at x=0.\n\n# FUNDAMENTAL PROBLEM with psi = sqrt(1+t^2) - sqrt(1+x^2):\n# psi_xx < 0 means c^2*psi_xx contributes positively to L1+L through alpha term.\n\n# We need both psi_tt > 0 AND psi_xx > 0 for the approach to work.\n# But for a function of x alone with psi_xx > 0 everywhere:\n# f''(x) > 0 means f is convex, hence f(x) -> +inf as x -> ±inf.\n# Then -f(x) -> -inf as x -> +inf, so lam*psi involves lam*(-f(x)).\n# With lam < 0: lam*(-f(x)) = |lam|*f(x) -> +inf. ✓ for condition 2.\n# \n# So psi = g(t) - f(x) with g'' > 0 (convex), f'' > 0 (convex).\n# Example: f(x) = sqrt(1+x^2), f'' = 1/(1+x^2)^(3/2) > 0 ✓\n#          g(t) = sqrt(1+t^2), g'' = 1/(1+t^2)^(3/2) > 0 ✓\n# \n# Wait, psi = g - f, so psi_xx = -f''(x) < 0! Not > 0!\n# We need the NEGATIVE of a convex function for the x part.\n# \n# psi = g(t) + h(x) where h''(x) > 0.\n# Then psi_x = h'(x), psi_xx = h''(x) > 0.\n# But we need lam*psi -> +inf as x -> inf.\n# psi ~ h(x) as x -> inf. With h convex: h(x) -> +inf.\n# lam*psi ~ lam*h(x). With lam < 0: -> -inf. BAD.\n# With lam > 0: -> +inf. ✓\n#\n# So try lam > 0!\n# Then condition 2: lam*psi = lam*(g(t)+h(x)) -> +inf as x->inf iff h(x)->inf. ✓\n# L1/phi = lam^2*(g'^2 + c^2*h'^2) + lam*(g'' + c^2*h'')\n# All terms positive! L1 > 0.\n# For condition 1: L1 <= L <= -L1 means L1 <= 0 (since L1 ≤ L ≤ -L1 implies L1 ≤ -L1 => 2L1 ≤ 0).\n# But L1 > 0. 